sequenceDiagram
    participant C1 as Caller 1 (lock holder)
    participant C2 as Caller 2 (spin-waiter)
    participant C3 as Caller N (spin-waiter)
    participant R as Redis

    Note over C1,C3: All request same key — cache miss

    C1->>R: GET key
    C2->>R: GET key
    C3->>R: GET key
    R-->>C1: miss (nil)
    R-->>C2: miss (nil)
    R-->>C3: miss (nil)

    C1->>R: SETNX key:lock token (lock acquired)
    R-->>C1: true
    C2->>R: SETNX key:lock
    R-->>C2: false
    C3->>R: SETNX key:lock
    R-->>C3: false

    Note over C1: Lock holder path
    C1->>R: GET key (double-check)
    R-->>C1: miss (nil)
    C1->>C1: fn() — compute value (DB query / API call)
    C1->>R: SET key value TTL
    C1->>R: DEL key:lock if value == token (release lock)
    C1-->>C1: return value

    Note over C2,C3: Spin-wait path
    loop up to ~500ms
        C2->>R: GET key
        C3->>R: GET key
        Note over C2: exponential backoff 5ms→50ms
    end
    R-->>C2: value
    R-->>C3: value
    C2-->>C2: return value
    C3-->>C3: return value

    Note over C1,C3: All 3 callers get result. fn() called once.
